course: dictionary
lesson: 11512
title: Airy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Airy is an adjective. It describes things that feel full of fresh air, light and open. «The classroom had tall windows and felt bright and airy.» Airy tells you the room was open and full of fresh air, not stuffy or dark.
explain: Airy can also mean light and delicate, like air itself. «The chef served a light, airy mousse.» A mousse is soft and fluffy, so airy means it is light, as if it is full of tiny bubbles of air. Ask yourself: is this thing light or heavy?
explain: Airy can describe a way of speaking or acting too. «She gave an airy wave and said, "Don't worry about it."» Here airy means careless, not serious. The wave shows she is not bothered at all. Look at the clues around the word to choose the right meaning.
explain: Be careful with airy-fairy. This is an informal British phrase meaning vague and unrealistic. «His airy-fairy plans never worked.» The clue is that the plans never worked, so they were not practical.
fact: Airy is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a room, some bread or a reply.
fact: «Airy» means full of fresh air and space, light and open.
fact: «Airy» can also mean light and delicate, like air.
fact: «Airy» can mean not serious or careless, as in «an airy wave of the hand».
fact: Airy-fairy is British informal slang meaning vague and unrealistic.
exercise: «The classroom was bright and airy, with big open windows.» What does airy mean here? | *Full of fresh air and space | Full of paint | Very noisy | Dark and cold
exercise: «The bread was light and airy, with lots of tiny holes.» What does airy describe? | Sweet and sticky | Hard and sharp | Heavy and wet | *Light, like air
exercise: «He gave an airy reply, as if the test did not matter at all.» Which word is closest in meaning to airy here? | tired | angry | *careless | loud
test: Which meaning fits «a bright, airy kitchen»? | Smelly and hot | *Full of fresh air, light and open | Dark and crowded
test: Jen says, «Your plan is airy-fairy.» What does she mean? | *Vague and unrealistic | Happy and bouncy | Full of air bubbles | Very organised and detailed
exam: Which sentence best shows that airy means light and delicate? | «He shouted an angry answer.» | «The road was muddy and wet.» | «The box was heavy and full of bricks.» | *«The angel's wings looked light and airy as a feather.»
